My topic is ChatGPT as a coding partner. I will test how well ChatGPT can solve 20 beginner-level programming problems.
I will give ChatGPT twenty programming tasks that come from LeetCode Easy-level questions. These tasks will include arrays, strings, loops, sorting, searching, and simple logic. I will test each solution to see whether ChatGPT answers on the first try. I will record the results. Calculate ChatGPT's overall accuracy. I will also look for mistakes, such as logic errors, indexing errors, and failures to handle special cases.

This topic matters because many students and programmers use ChatGPT to help them write and understand code. ChatGPT can save time, explain concepts and help beginners learn programming. However AI-generated code is not always correct. Sometimes the code looks right. Fails when tested with inputs.
By testing ChatGPT with twenty programming problems I can understand how reliable ChatGPT is as a coding assistant. This research will also show why programmers should test and review AI-generated code of trusting every answer. ChatGPT should help people learn programming, not replace their problem-solving skills.


How accurately can ChatGPT solve twenty beginner-level programming problems on its attempt and what coding mistakes does ChatGPT make often?
I will give ChatGPT each problem without hints. Test its solution. Each correct solution will receive one point while incorrect solutions will receive zero points. I will calculate ChatGPTs accuracy by dividing the number of answers by twenty.
